<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arcesilaus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 550 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Arcesilaus II of Cyrene, Arcesilaus the Harsh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arcesilaus II, called 'the Harsh', was the fourth king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battiad-dynasty">Battiad dynasty</a> of Cyrene in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> in the mid-6th century BCE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, a quarrel with his brothers led them to leave Cyrene and found the city of Barca inland. He was later defeated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libyans">Libyans</a> at Leucon and was strangled by his brother Learchus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arcesilaus-ii.jpg" alt="Arcesilaus II" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ArchaiOptix · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arkesilas_Painter_-_Arkesilas_supervising_the_silphion_trade_-_Paris_BnF_CabMed_189_-_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
